00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.870 align:start position:0%
 
who edits my videos  so i got a great question for one of my  loyal youtube viewers love you guys  leonardo who wrote in to say what's up  evan who edits your videos what's up leo  if you want to know what's up you can  check out my what's up video and in  terms of who edits my videos i want to  tell you a quick story that i hope will  help see i'm a big believer in not  spending money until i'm making money  for those of you loyal youtube viewers  you'll know what i'm talking about it's  a message i repeat in a lot of my videos  when i started my youtube channel i  wanted to have a place to have a greater  impact and help people in a visual way  but i wasn't making any money at it so i  didn't want to spend anything i didn't  spend on editing i didn't spend on gear  i didn't spend it on anything but i was  willing to invest my time and my hustle  so stage one for me was actually  partnering up a buddy of mine named mark  drager runs a video production company  called phantom media he's been on the  channel a few times i've interviewed him  and we started together where i would be  on camera and he would film it and edit  it and produce it and then i would  publish it to the channel he did it  because i guess he wanted to be a friend  to me and he also saw a promotional  angle to get some exposure for his  business but after a while it got to be  too taxing for mark and his team to  handle i was making too many videos and  he wasn't i guess seen enough of return  to continue on with me i still wasn't  making enough money to justify hiring an  editor so my stage two was i did it  myself now i was by no means a video  editor i had no skills no training  didn't know what i was doing i started  by using windows movie maker and a lot  of the early videos on my channel are me  editing my windows movie maker videos as  i needed more features and i learned a  little bit more about video editing  software i picked up camtasia and  started using that as my default editor  but i was still doing all the work  myself as i built up my audience and i  started getting a little bit of traction  with the channel  a big company in the telecommunications  space said they wanted to work with me  on a video they gave me a little bit of  a budget to play with and now that i was  making some money from my channel i  could afford to invest it back into the  channel so one of the first things i did  was put out a job on odesk and i hired  my first video editor sa'ad and saad was  great and reliable and i would upload  the videos to him on dropbox he would  send them back to me and i would put  them up on my channel and then one day  sa'ad poof  disappeared and now suddenly i was stuck  having to edit all these videos myself  and it really sucks as an entrepreneur  when you hire somebody and you finally  give away those responsibilities  that you don't want to have anymore  yourself and then you have to take them  back on you really really really don't  want to do them saad went from being  super reliable to not responding to any  email for two weeks so i said enough is  enough i have to go find somebody new to  help me edit these videos because i  can't keep doing this myself and that's  where i found christina  christina say hi  and christina's been doing a fantastic  job for me she's been editing all the  videos she's been posting them to  youtube she's been adding in the title  in the description and saved a lot of my  time so that i can spend more of my time  being in front of the camera instead of  being in front of the computer editing  them now i later found out that sa'ad  actually got kidnapped and he was out  for two months and held for ransom and i  guess that was something that was  relatively normal in his country but by  the time he came back i had christina  who was doing an amazing job and who i  wanted to keep on board on my team so  those are my three steps i started with  alliance partners then i started doing  it myself and then as i started making  money from my channel i was able to go  out and hire somebody to help me do it i  hope that answers your question leonardo  believe  for those of you watching i would love  for you to tell me who your first hire  was what their role was i don't care  about their name but what was their role  what what job function did they have in  your business or if you're thinking  about hiring somebody who's the first  person that you want to hire for your  business to take some stuff off your  plate leave in the comments below i'm  really curious to see what you guys are  thinking and of course if you like this  video and you want to see more don't  forget to subscribe to the channel and  to the newsletter thank you so much for  watching i'll see you soon

